  "proof_summary": [
    "The literal physical unit point and canonical unit point remain distinct. Real endpoint metadata plus full stored-field identities give a global equality for each of the ten actual atoms.",
    "Actual positive Jacobian and two inverse identities give chi_prime=1/Y_prime_at_chi and reciprocalYprime=chi_prime_at_Y. The canonical source factor is H(chi)*chi_prime; its inverse is reciprocalH(chi)*Y_prime(chi).",
    "Global regularity of the supplied reference cylinder implies global smoothness of every displayed scalar. Its radial lift is periodic and all mixed jets reduce to the genuine scalar jets.",
    "The exact finite-prefix102 material bound uses the original width bound and the same Y/H/positive inverse jets. Packing (M*C0^M)*E0^M requires the explicit actual normalized sample E0>=1.",
    "For every order the numerical constant precedes the underlying K,enumeration,relative fields,component and point. Only the positive fields of the true n04WholeReferenceGaugeAtlasData are used; the negative K is never replaced.",
    "The generic actual-atom identity and scalar regularity are public for the subsequent left/nu source-column consumers, avoiding a second expansion of the true source formula."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "No new reference family, interpolation width, cell, material data or low finite envelope is selected.",
    "This fixed-family consumer obtains its inputs from the same single276 family and retained finite certificate; it does not manufacture those costs from arbitrary qualitative geometry.",
    "Only the ten displayed positive geometry atoms are handled. Five principal/potential atoms are supplied by the independently reviewed companion family. No negative-side or complete terminal ReferenceJets claim.",
    "No local compilation/elaboration, resource-limit change, active source/index/ref edit or CI request."
